<!DOCTYPE html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<pre class="metadata">
title: Intl.LocaleMatcher
stage: 1
contributors: Ecma International, Long Ho
location: https://tc39.es/proposal-intl-localematcher/
</pre>
<emu-biblio href="./node_modules/@tc39/ecma262-biblio/biblio.json"></emu-biblio>
<emu-biblio href="./node_modules/@tc39/ecma402-biblio/biblio.json"></emu-biblio>

<emu-intro id="sec-introduction">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p>This working draft prepares application-supplied locales once and selects one resource, one resource per request, or all acceptable resources without implicit defaulting. Best-fit policy and data remain implementation-defined.</p>
  <p>In <a href="https://tc39.es/ecma402/#sec-constructor-properties-of-the-intl-object">Constructor Properties of the Intl Object</a>, add Intl.LocaleMatcher and exclude it, alongside Intl.Locale, from the service constructors. It matches application resources rather than negotiating an implementation's supported services.</p>
</emu-intro>

<emu-clause id="sec-locale-matching-operation-changes">
  <h1>Changes to Locale Matching Operations</h1>
  <p>Extend the result Records of LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix and LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit with a [[requestedLocale]] field. Its value is the element of the requested Language Priority List whose selection produced the match, before removing its Unicode locale extension sequence.</p>
  <p>In LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix, at the beginning of each iteration over _requestedLocales_, let _requestedLocale_ be _locale_. When returning a matching Record, include [[requestedLocale]]: _requestedLocale_ alongside [[locale]] and [[extension]].</p>
  <p>LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit must return the corresponding selected request in [[requestedLocale]]. Selection still considers the whole requested Language Priority List; adding this field does not change matching policy. Calls that find no match continue to return *undefined*.</p>
  <p>For best fit, a selected available/requested pair must be accepted by BestFitLocaleMatch. Acceptance is independent of available-list order, other candidates, and request-list priority penalties. With singleton available and requested lists, LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit returns a match if and only if BestFitLocaleMatch accepts that pair. Selection among acceptable pairs remains implementation-defined.</p>

  <emu-clause id="sec-bestfitlocalematch" type="abstract operation" aoid="BestFitLocaleMatch">
    <h1>BestFitLocaleMatch ( _availableLocale_, _requestedLocale_ )</h1>
    <p>The implementation-defined abstract operation BestFitLocaleMatch takes arguments _availableLocale_ (a Unicode canonicalized locale identifier without a Unicode locale extension sequence) and _requestedLocale_ (a Unicode canonicalized locale identifier) and returns a Boolean. It determines whether _availableLocale_ is an acceptable resource for _requestedLocale_, using the same pairwise acceptance policy as LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit and ignoring the requested Unicode locale extension sequence. The policy may be directional. No data source, distance scale, or numeric threshold is required.</p>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-createlocalematchresult" type="abstract operation" aoid="CreateLocaleMatchResult">
    <h1>CreateLocaleMatchResult ( _locale_, _requestedLocale_ )</h1>
    <p>The abstract operation CreateLocaleMatchResult takes arguments _locale_ (a String) and _requestedLocale_ (a String) and returns an Object. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
    <emu-alg>
      1. Let _result_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(%Object.prototype%).
      1. Perform ! CreateDataPropertyOrThrow(_result_, *"locale"*, _locale_).
      1. Perform ! CreateDataPropertyOrThrow(_result_, *"requestedLocale"*, _requestedLocale_).
      1. Return _result_.
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-clause>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="localematcher-objects">
  <h1>LocaleMatcher Objects</h1>
  <p>The objects and functions defined here follow ECMA-402's <a href="https://tc39.es/ecma402/#requirements">requirements for standard built-in ECMAScript objects</a>.</p>

  <emu-clause id="sec-intl-localematcher-constructor">
    <h1>The Intl.LocaleMatcher Constructor</h1>
    <p>The Intl.LocaleMatcher constructor is <dfn>%Intl.LocaleMatcher%</dfn>, the initial value of the *"LocaleMatcher"* property of the Intl object.</p>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher ( _availableLocales_ [ , _options_ ] )</h1>
      <emu-alg>
        1. If NewTarget is *undefined*, throw a *TypeError* exception.
        1. Let _slots_ be « [[InitializedLocaleMatcher]], [[AvailableLocales]], [[LocaleMatcher]] ».
        1. Let _matcher_ be ? OrdinaryCreateFromConstructor(NewTarget, *"%Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype%"*, _slots_).
        1. Let _available_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_availableLocales_).
        1. For each element _locale_ of _available_, do
          1. If _locale_ contains a Unicode locale extension sequence, throw a *RangeError* exception.
        1. Set _options_ to ? GetOptionsObject(_options_).
        1. Let _algorithm_ be ? GetOption(_options_, *"algorithm"*, ~string~, « *"lookup"*, *"best fit"* », *"best fit"*).
        1. Set _matcher_.[[AvailableLocales]] to _available_.
        1. Set _matcher_.[[LocaleMatcher]] to _algorithm_.
        1. Set _matcher_.[[InitializedLocaleMatcher]] to *true*.
        1. Return _matcher_.
      </emu-alg>
      <p>The *"length"* property of Intl.LocaleMatcher is *1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
      <emu-note>
        Available locales describe app resources. No host default, parent tags, or Intl service support is required. CanonicalizeLocaleList copies and deduplicates them; later input or option mutations do not change the matcher. Implementations may prepare reusable indices, without a required technique or timing guarantee.
      </emu-note>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-intl-localematcher-constructor">
    <h1>Properties of the Intl.LocaleMatcher Constructor</h1>
    <p>The constructor has a [[Prototype]] internal slot whose value is %Function.prototype%.</p>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype</h1>
      <p>The value of this property is %Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype%.</p>
      <p>This property has the attributes { [[Writable]]: *false*, [[Enumerable]]: *false*, [[Configurable]]: *false* }.</p>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-intl-localematcher-prototype-object">
    <h1>Properties of the Intl.LocaleMatcher Prototype Object</h1>
    <p>The prototype object is <dfn>%Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype%</dfn>, an ordinary object with [[Prototype]] %Object.prototype%. It is not a LocaleMatcher instance and has none of the instance internal slots.</p>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype.constructor">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype.constructor</h1>
      <p>The initial value is %Intl.LocaleMatcher%.</p>
    </emu-clause>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype.match">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype.match ( _requestedLocales_ )</h1>
      <emu-alg>
        1. Let _matcher_ be the *this* value.
        1. Perform ? RequireInternalSlot(_matcher_, [[InitializedLocaleMatcher]]).
        1. Let _requested_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_requestedLocales_).
        1. Let _available_ be _matcher_.[[AvailableLocales]].
        1. If _requested_ is empty or _available_ is empty, return *undefined*.
        1. If _matcher_.[[LocaleMatcher]] is *"lookup"*, then
          1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix(_available_, _requested_).
        1. Else,
          1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit(_available_, _requested_).
        1. If _match_ is *undefined*, return *undefined*.
        1. Return CreateLocaleMatchResult(_match_.[[locale]], _match_.[[requestedLocale]]).
      </emu-alg>
      <p>The *"length"* property of this method is *1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
      <p>Each successful call returns a fresh ordinary object. Its *"locale"* property is an element of [[AvailableLocales]]. Its *"requestedLocale"* property is the canonical selected request, including its extensions. Both properties are writable, enumerable, and configurable.</p>
      <emu-note>
        Each call validates the complete request list, even with no available locales. No match returns undefined; callers can apply their own fallback. This method does not call DefaultLocale. Requested Unicode locale extensions are ignored during matching and retained in *"requestedLocale"*; they are not appended to *"locale"*. Neither property is a synthesized formatting locale.
      </emu-note>
      <emu-note>
        Best fit uses the existing ECMA-402 operation, with no required CLDR/ICU data, scoring, expansion, penalty, or tie policy. Other extensions and private-use subtags retain that operation's treatment; no application-specific meaning is assigned.
      </emu-note>
    </emu-clause>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype.matchall">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype.matchAll ( _requestedLocales_ )</h1>
      <emu-alg>
        1. Let _matcher_ be the *this* value.
        1. Perform ? RequireInternalSlot(_matcher_, [[InitializedLocaleMatcher]]).
        1. Let _requested_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_requestedLocales_).
        1. Let _available_ be _matcher_.[[AvailableLocales]].
        1. Let _results_ be a new empty List.
        1. Let _seen_ be a new empty List.
        1. For each element _requestedLocale_ of _requested_, do
          1. If _matcher_.[[LocaleMatcher]] is *"lookup"*, then
            1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix(_available_, « _requestedLocale_ »).
          1. Else,
            1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit(_available_, « _requestedLocale_ »).
          1. If _match_ is not *undefined* and _seen_ does not contain _match_.[[locale]], then
            1. Append _match_.[[locale]] to _seen_.
            1. Append CreateLocaleMatchResult(_match_.[[locale]], _match_.[[requestedLocale]]) to _results_.
        1. Return CreateArrayFromList(_results_).
      </emu-alg>
      <p>The *"length"* property of this method is *1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
      <emu-note>
        Each request is matched independently against the full available list. Results follow request order, with duplicate resources omitted after their first occurrence. A duplicate does not trigger a search for another resource. An empty input or no match returns a fresh empty Array. The first result need not equal match's whole-list best-fit selection.
      </emu-note>
    </emu-clause>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype.filter">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype.filter ( _requestedLocales_ )</h1>
      <emu-alg>
        1. Let _matcher_ be the *this* value.
        1. Perform ? RequireInternalSlot(_matcher_, [[InitializedLocaleMatcher]]).
        1. Let _requested_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_requestedLocales_).
        1. Let _available_ be _matcher_.[[AvailableLocales]].
        1. Let _results_ be a new empty List.
        1. Let _seen_ be a new empty List.
        1. For each element _requestedLocale_ of _requested_, do
          1. For each element _availableLocale_ of _available_, do
            1. If _seen_ does not contain _availableLocale_, then
              1. If _matcher_.[[LocaleMatcher]] is *"lookup"*, then
                1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix(« _availableLocale_ », « _requestedLocale_ »).
                1. Let _accepted_ be *false*.
                1. If _match_ is not *undefined*, set _accepted_ to *true*.
              1. Else,
                1. Let _accepted_ be BestFitLocaleMatch(_availableLocale_, _requestedLocale_).
              1. If _accepted_ is *true*, then
                1. Append _availableLocale_ to _seen_.
                1. Append CreateLocaleMatchResult(_availableLocale_, _requestedLocale_) to _results_.
        1. Return CreateArrayFromList(_results_).
      </emu-alg>
      <p>The *"length"* property of this method is *1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
      <emu-note>
        Returns every acceptable available resource once, grouped by the earliest request that accepts it. Within each group, available-list order is preserved. This is not a ranking by linguistic distance. Lookup acceptance uses prefix lookup against each candidate alone; it does not use RFC 4647 filtering. An empty input or no match returns a fresh empty Array.
      </emu-note>
    </emu-clause>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype-tostringtag">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype [ %Symbol.toStringTag% ]</h1>
      <p>The initial value is *"Intl.LocaleMatcher"*.</p>
      <p>This property has the attributes { [[Writable]]: *false*, [[Enumerable]]: *false*, [[Configurable]]: *true* }.</p>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-intl-localematcher-instances">
    <h1>Properties of Intl.LocaleMatcher Instances</h1>
    <p>Instances are ordinary objects with these internal slots:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>[[InitializedLocaleMatcher]]: *true*.</li>
      <li>[[AvailableLocales]]: the private Available Locales List copied during construction.</li>
      <li>[[LocaleMatcher]]: *"lookup"* or *"best fit"*.</li>
    </ul>
  </emu-clause>
</emu-clause>
